                    </div>
                    
                    <p>That is clustering at work. It is like a party planner, grouping together songs you like so it can suggest similar ones.</p>
                    
                    <div class=\"info-box\">
                        <h3>Finding Natural Groupings</h3>
                        <p>Clustering algorithms identify natural groups or patterns in data without being told in advance what those groups should be (unsupervised learning). They group items based on how similar they are to each other.</p>
                        <p>Popular clustering algorithms include:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>K-means:</strong> Divides data into a specified number of clusters</li>
                            <li><strong>Hierarchical Clustering:</strong> Creates a tree of clusters</li>
                            <li><strong>DBSCAN:</strong> Groups data based on density</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>Beyond music recommendations, clustering is used for customer segmentation, image compression, anomaly detection, and document organization.</p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section class=\"content-section\" id=\"optimization\">
                    <h2>Optimization Algorithms: Finding the Best Solution</h2>
                    <p>And when you are hungry and waiting for your food delivery, an optimization algorithm is finding the quickest route to get your food to you.</p>
                    
                    <div class=\"image-container\">
