                        <p class=\"caption\">Optimization algorithms find the most efficient solution, like determining the fastest delivery route among multiple possibilities.</p>
                    </div>
                    
                    <p>It is like a navigator, always searching for the best solution. These optimization algorithms don\'t just find any solution - they find the best one according to specific criteria, such as the shortest time or distance.</p>
                    
                    <div class=\"key-concept\">
                        <h3>Finding the Optimal Solution</h3>
                        <p>Optimization algorithms aim to find the best possible solution to a problem from a range of possible solutions. They are essential for problems with many possible answers where we need to find the \"best\" one based on certain criteria.</p>
                        <p>Common applications include:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Route planning for deliveries or transportation</li>
                            <li>Resource allocation in manufacturing</li>
                            <li>Schedule optimization for staff, flights, or classes</li>
                            <li>Portfolio optimization in finance</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    
                    <p>Data scientists use these and other types of algorithms to make sense of the world around us. They are like the secret superheroes of the digital age, using their powers to make our lives easier and more convenient. And the best part? These algorithms are getting more advanced every day, learning from the vast amounts of data we generate.</p>
                </section>
            </div>', '109', '15', '1', '2025-11-04 14:58:16', '2025-11-04 14:58:16');
INSERT INTO `lessons` (`id`, `module_id`, `title`, `subtitle`, `slug`, `content`, `order_index`, `duration_minutes`, `is_published`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES ('11', '1', 'Chapter 1.10: AI in Action', 'Exploring how AI systems work together in real-world applications', 'chapter11', '<div class=\"chapter-content\">
                <section class=\"content-section\" id=\"introduction\">
                    <h2>AI Systems Working Together</h2>
                    <p>Machine learning and deep learning use specific algorithms to learn from vast amounts of data and complete tasks. But how does it all fit together in AI systems like robots, and self-driving cars? Let\'s explore.</p>
                    
                    <div class=\"image-container\">
                        <svg width=\"400\" height=\"220\" viewbox=\"0 0 400 220\">
                            <!-- Robot Illustration -->
                            <rect x=\"80\" y=\"80\" width=\"40\" height=\"50\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#333\"></rect>
