                        </svg>
                        <p class=\"caption\">Robotic systems in manufacturing collect data from every movement and interaction, which AI algorithms use to optimize operations.</p>
                    </div>
                    
                    <p>Every movement, interaction, and task a robot performs can be translated into valuable data. The internet is not just about your smartphone or laptop. It is much more expansive.</p>
                    
                    <div class=\"key-concept\">
                        <h3>Robots as Data Collectors and Actors</h3>
                        <p>Modern robots are not just mechanical devices - they are sophisticated AI systems that:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Collect data</strong> through sensors (cameras, microphones, pressure sensors, etc.)</li>
                            <li><strong>Process information</strong> using machine learning algorithms</li>
                            <li><strong>Make decisions</strong> based on programming and learned patterns</li>
                            <li><strong>Take physical actions</strong> in the real world</li>
                            <li><strong>Adapt over time</strong> as they gather more experience data</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section class=\"content-section\" id=\"smart-homes\">
                    <h2>Smart Home Automation</h2>
                    <p>From connected homes to smart appliances, the internet is everywhere. The Internet of Things has woven itself into our everyday lives, making our homes smarter and more responsive to our needs.</p>
                    
