                    </div>

                    <div class=\"key-concept\">
                        <h3>Major Generative AI Model Types</h3>
                        <p>Several key types of generative models power today\'s AI applications:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Generative Pre-trained Transformers (GPT):</strong> Language models that generate natural, context-aware text based on prompts</li>
                            <li><strong>Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs):</strong> Models consisting of two neural networks—a generator and discriminator—that compete to create realistic images</li>
                            <li><strong>Diffusion Models:</strong> Create images by gradually removing noise from random data, now powering many image generation tools</li>
                            <li><strong>Variational Autoencoders (VAEs):</strong> Models that compress data to its essential features and then generate new examples from this compressed representation</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    
                    <p>The Generative Pre-Trained Transformer, or GPT model is one such example. GPT models can understand context and make predictions, which is why they are used in applications like text completion, translation, and even coding assistance.</p>
                    
                    <div class=\"info-box\">
                        <h3>Spotlight: GPT Models</h3>
                        <p>GPT (Generative Pre-trained Transformer) is a family of language models that use deep learning techniques to generate natural language text. These models are called \"transformers\" because of their architectural design, which uses a mechanism called \"attention\" to understand context across long passages of text.</p>
                        <p>Key characteristics of GPT models include:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>They are pre-trained on vast amounts of text from the internet</li>
                            <li>They can be fine-tuned for specific tasks</li>
                            <li>They generate text by predicting the next word in a sequence</li>
                            <li>Each new version (GPT-3, GPT-4, etc.) has increased size and capabilities</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section class=\"content-section\" id=\"model-architecture\">
                    <h2>Model Architecture and Training</h2>
                    <p>Understanding the architecture of generative AI models helps explain how they work and what makes them capable of creating such impressive outputs.</p>
                    
