                    <div class=\"info-box\">
                        <h3>How Users Engage with AI Models</h3>
                        <p>Most people interact with generative AI models through:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Web Interfaces:</strong> Services like Microsoft Copilot, DALL-E, or ChatGPT provide easy-to-use web interfaces</li>
                            <li><strong>Mobile Apps:</strong> Smartphone applications that provide access to AI capabilities</li>
                            <li><strong>Integrated Tools:</strong> AI features built into software like Microsoft 365 or Google Workspace</li>
                            <li><strong>API Access:</strong> For developers who want to build custom applications using AI models</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>These interfaces typically allow users to provide prompts (instructions or questions) and receive the AI\'s generated responses, whether they\'re text, images, code, or other formats.</p>
                    </div>
                    
                    <p>For those without technical expertise, generative AI is accessible through services like Microsoft Copilot, which handles the complex interactions with the underlying models. This approach allows anyone to benefit from AI capabilities without needing to understand the technical details of how the models work.</p>
                </section>

