                            <rect x=\"50\" y=\"210\" width=\"300\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#F0F0F0\" stroke=\"#333\" rx=\"5\"></rect>
                            <text x=\"200\" y=\"223\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-size=\"8\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Trained on Millions of Text-Image Pairs</text>
                            
                            <text x=\"200\" y=\"25\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">How Text-to-Image Generation Works</text>
                        </svg>
                        <p class=\"caption\">Text-to-image generators transform text descriptions into visual content through multiple processing stages, trained on millions of examples.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class=\"info-box\">
                        <h3>How Text-to-Image AI Works</h3>
                        <p>The process of generating images from text typically follows these steps:</p>
                        <ol>
                            <li><strong>Text Encoding:</strong> The system analyzes and encodes the text description, identifying key concepts, objects, attributes, and relationships</li>
                            <li><strong>Latent Space Mapping:</strong> The encoded text is mapped to a \"latent space\" where textual concepts have visual correspondences</li>
                            <li><strong>Image Generation:</strong> Using techniques like diffusion models or GANs, the system progressively generates an image that matches the text description</li>
                            <li><strong>Refinement:</strong> The generated image may go through refinement stages to improve quality and more closely match the prompt</li>
                        </ol>
                        <p>This entire process relies on massive datasets of text-image pairs that the AI has been trained on, enabling it to understand the relationships between language descriptions and visual elements.</p>
                    </div>
                    
                    <p>The quality of your prompt greatly influences the resulting image. Detailed, specific prompts generally produce better results than vague ones. For example, \"A digital illustration of a beach scene crafted from yarn. The sandy beach is depicted with beige yarn, waves are made of blue and white yarn crashing onto the shore. A yarn sun sets on the horizon, casting a warm glow\" would yield a more precise result than simply \"a beach made of yarn.\"</p>
                </section>

                <section class=\"content-section\" id=\"dalle\">
                    <h2>DALL·E: Pioneering Text-to-Image AI</h2>
                    <p>DALL·E, an AI model developed by OpenAI, is an example of this technology. It can generate detailed images from simple descriptions, effectively translating words into visual representations. This model is also integrated into Microsoft Designer, which is a feature within Image Creator in Microsoft Copilot.</p>
                    
