                    <div class=\"info-box\">
                        <h3>Using Microsoft Designer in Copilot</h3>
                        <p>To create images with Microsoft Copilot:</p>
                        <ol>
                            <li><strong>Navigate to Microsoft Copilot:</strong> Visit the copilot.microsoft.com website</li>
                            <li><strong>Select Creative Style:</strong> Choose the \"More Creative\" conversation style for image creation</li>
                            <li><strong>Craft Your Prompt:</strong> Write a detailed description of the image you want to create</li>
                            <li><strong>Use Clear Instructions:</strong> Start with phrases like \"Create an image of...\" to ensure Copilot understands you want an image</li>
                            <li><strong>Generate the Image:</strong> Click the Generate arrow and wait for your image to be created</li>
                            <li><strong>Refine if Needed:</strong> You can request modifications to the generated image with follow-up prompts</li>
                        </ol>
                    </div>
                    
                    <p>Remember, the more detailed and descriptive your prompt, the more accurate the generated image will be. So, don\'t hesitate to add more specifics about the image you want to create. If the image isn\'t quite what you want, you can ask Microsoft Copilot to edit your image with additional details like \"Add a city background.\"</p>
                </section>

                <section class=\"content-section\" id=\"use-cases\">
