        <h3>Global Recommendations</h3>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Encourage Data Sharing While Safeguarding Privacy:</strong> This balance is important for improving AI systems without compromising individual rights</li>
            <li><strong>Invest in AI Research:</strong> Continued research will fuel innovation and ensure that the benefits of AI are accessible to all</li>
            <li><strong>Promote Digital Education and Workforce Development:</strong> As AI transforms the job market, we need to equip people with the skills to thrive in this new landscape</li>
            <li><strong>Establish AI Advisory Committees:</strong> Organizations and communities should create committees to provide oversight and guidance about AI systems</li>
            <li><strong>Engage with Government Officials:</strong> They play a crucial role in shaping policies that affect AI use in communities</li>
            <li><strong>Regulate AI Based on Broad Principles:</strong> This approach allows for flexibility as AI technologies evolve, while ensuring they uphold shared values</li>
        </ol>
        
        <div class=\"key-concept\">
            <h3>Human-AI Collaboration</h3>
            <p>The future of AI isn\'t about replacement, but collaboration. By designing AI systems that complement human abilities, we can create solutions that are more powerful than either humans or AI could achieve alone. This requires thoughtful design of human-AI interfaces and workflows that leverage the strengths of both.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

