        <h3>Microsoft\'s Responsible AI Standard</h3>
        <p>Microsoft has taken several steps to ensure that AI systems are used responsibly, such as creating guidelines known as the Responsible AI Standard. This standard ensures that AI systems are:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Fair:</strong> Treating all users equitably without discrimination</li>
            <li><strong>Safe:</strong> Designed to prevent harm and maintain security</li>
            <li><strong>Private:</strong> Respecting user data and privacy rights</li>
            <li><strong>Inclusive:</strong> Designed for accessibility and usability by all</li>
            <li><strong>Transparent:</strong> Operating in ways that are understandable to users</li>
            <li><strong>Accountable:</strong> Having clear lines of responsibility and oversight</li>
        </ul>
        
        <p>To predict and reduce any unfair impacts from AI systems, a method called measurement modeling is used. This helps in identifying potential issues before they become a problem.</p>
        
        <h3>Bias Detection Tools</h3>
        <p>Understanding how an AI makes decisions can be complex. Companies are developing tools to detect societal bias in AI algorithms. These tools will alert us if an AI system might be unfairly favoring certain groups over others.</p>
        
